  <item>
    <title>Gorham: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/gorham-me</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-gorham-me</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>180-day moratorium on data center development, adopted 7-0 in June 2026. Councilors voted unanimously in Nov 2026 for another 180 days, to May 2027; the exact end date was not published in the coverage read. A permanent ban is still under consideration</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Scarborough: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/scarborough-me</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-scarborough-me</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Town Council voted unanimously on Nov 4, 2026 for a zoning amendment under which data centers are not permitted in any zoning district, effective immediately; accessory server rooms remain allowed. Replaces the 180-day moratorium adopted in June 2026</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Westbrook: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/westbrook-me</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-westbrook-me</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>City Council voted unanimously on Nov 2, 2026 to amend the land use ordinance, removing data centers from the Rock Row Contract Zone, the only zone that permitted them. Standalone data centers are now prohibited; data centers remain allowed only as an accessory use. Follows the 180-day moratorium adopted in June 2026</description>
  </item>
